# Cargo test gate

When verifying Rust changes (compiler, VM, parser, CLI, or CI), **do not** run bare `cargo test` or package-only suites as the sole check.

## Required local / agent commands

```bash
cargo test --workspace --lib --tests --bins
```

Retry once on transient macOS/EAGAIN listing failures (same as CI).
Reactor pool size defaults to `1` under cargo (`COIL_MAX_WORKER_THREADS` in `.cargo/config.toml`) and when `CI` is set (`WorkerCap`).

Prefer `--lib --tests --bins` over `--all-targets`: Criterion `[[bench]]` targets treat argv after `--` as their own CLI and abort the suite. Integration tests under `*/tests/` (e.g. `compiler/tests/diagnostics.rs`, `pipeline.rs`, `perf_metrics.rs`) are covered by `--tests`.

## Feature-gated suites

| Feature | Command | Notes |
|---------|---------|--------|
| default stack | `cargo test --workspace --lib --tests --bins` | full suite |
| `no-default` | `cargo test --workspace --lib --tests --bins --no-default-features` | real suite; time tests are `cfg`-skipped |
| `crypto` / `time` | `cargo check --workspace --lib --tests --bins --no-default-features --features <name>` | CI compile-gate only; `crypto` is an empty leftover Cargo feature |
| `dissect` | `cargo test --workspace --lib --tests --bins --features dissect` | dissect integration |
| `debugger` | `cargo test --workspace --lib --tests --bins --features debugger` | debugger paths |

```bash
cargo test --workspace --lib --tests --bins --no-default-features
cargo check --workspace --lib --tests --bins --no-default-features --features time
cargo test --workspace --lib --tests --bins --features dissect
```

## Related gates

- Lint: `cargo check --workspace` (not clippy — `Gc::payload_mut` deny).
- Language harness (after a debug `coil` build): `./target/debug/coil test`.
